  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/thompson1917-ch14-10--gpt> a delphi:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "GPT-5.6 Sol on thompson1917-ch14-10: not-empirically-resolvable, resolvability 0.48" ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/dataset-resolvability-0.2.0> ;
    delphi:assessmentType "dataset-resolvability/0.2.0" ;
    delphi:hasScore "0.48"^^xsd:double ;
    delphi:hasVerdict "not-empirically-resolvable" ;
    delphi:hasConfidence "0.76"^^xsd:double ;
    dct:description "Existing plant data can refute or support specific adaptive explanations, but Thompson's unrestricted absence claim is not operationally bounded. Any observed pattern can be redescribed without settling whether it is 'significant.'" ;
    rdfs:comment "Proposed test with existing data: The mathematical convergence is demonstrable, but 'no biological significance' has no unique measurable consequence without specifying a biological function or causal model. Particular hypotheses, such as improved packing or light interception near the golden angle, can be tested, but no finite dataset can exclude every significance." ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/agent/delphisci-resolvability-assessor-gpt-5.6-sol-medium> ;
    delphi:evidenceAgainst "Biological significance is undefined and ranges over unlimited possible functions.", "The exact numerical convergence is a mathematical fact rather than an empirical claim." .
